FF]Clan-aware hint render path and clan summary hints[/bold #D7AFFF]            [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]plumbing[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]plumbing: thread HeaderHintState, the cached clan section snapshot, and [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]panel fold state through the clan branch of build_header_text into [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]build_clan_detail_text; stop the hint render from appending an agent [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]prompt tail or starting agent-header enrichment for synthetic clan rows;[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]give clans a bounded hint-render cache key; let hint-preserving repaints[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]and clan enrichment results reach clan containers; annotate the clan [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]summary block with span-preserving file hints.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  2 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Member-attributed clan body hints[/bold #D7AFFF]                             [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]sections[dim] · [dim][/dim]after plumbing[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]sections: annotate the visible bodies of the clan ERRORS, REPLIES, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]PROMPTS, and variable sections with file hints, resolving each fragment [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]against its own member's workspace and sharing one HintContentBudget [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]across the whole document, so hints exist exactly where text is visible [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]at the active fold level.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  3 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Structured SASE CONTEXT lane hints[/bold #D7AFFF]                            [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]context[dim] · [dim][/dim]after plumbing[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]context: register exact-path hints for individually rendered SASE [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]CONTEXT entries by reading the typed objects already carried on [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]ClanContextEntry.values, so PLAN, ARTIFACTS, and MEMORY entries hint [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]their real absolute paths instead of guessing from label text.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  4 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Clan slow tool call report hints[/bold #D7AFFF]                              [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]tools[dim] · [dim][/dim]after plumbing[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]tools: register tool-call report hints for the clan SLOW TOOL CALLS [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]section the same way the per-agent section does, so a hinted clan tool [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]call materializes a report file through the existing writer.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  5 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Clan commits lane and commit view hints[/bold #D7AFFF]                       [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]commits[dim] · [dim][/dim]after context[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]commits: aggregate member commits from already-loaded step output into a[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]new COMMITS context lane and register each rendered commit as a [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]commit-view hint so the clan document supports the commit viewer, raw [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]diff opening, and SHA copying.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  6 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Worker-resolved clan hint path index[/bold #D7AFFF]                          [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]resolve[dim] · [dim][/dim]after context, sections[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]resolve: compute a token-to-absolute-path index off-thread during clan [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]enrichment and consult it before workspace-relative fallback, so logical[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]plan references and other paths printed by clan summary scripts resolve [/#D7D7AF]\n